From 3e6601d66332eb10ae58c0478d8f39c3f2351758 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: will <will-tm@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 16:17:51 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 27/36] hw/display: a Vivante GC400T GPU the stock galcore
 stack draws with

The i.MX6SX GPU3D was a register stub that only reported an idle core, so
the flintstone's nlclient could not draw with its own libGAL/libEGL/
libGLESv2 and needed a replacement GL library in the guest. Model the GPU
instead, far enough for the vendor galcore 5.0.11 driver and its user
space to run unmodified:

- identity: the GC400T's model, revision and feature words;
- front end: galcore's END-terminated submissions and LINK/WAIT/CALL, with
  the fetch address galcore's idle check expects after an END; events
  raise the interrupt through AQIntrAcknowledge;
- MMU v1 and the memory base; tile status takes physical addresses;
- resolve engine: fills and copies between linear, tiled and supertiled
  surfaces with format conversion (frames reach the framebuffer this way,
  and libGAL's fences are small resolves);
- fast clear: tile status is resolved into the surfaces that are read;
- 3D: vertex fetch, a Vivante shader ISA interpreter (quads in lockstep,
  so derivatives and texture LOD work), clipping, the viewport, a
  top-left rasteriser over the scissor, perspective-correct varyings,
  texturing (the 8/16/32-bit formats, DXT, ETC1; linear, tiled and
  supertiled; nearest/linear/mipmaps), alpha test, depth/stencil,
  blending and the colour mask, with masked state writes as libGAL
  makes them. Rasterisation is split across host threads in bands of
  rows.

nlclient's screens render as on the device at ~50 frames a second while
animating. -global vivante-gc.trace=on logs register accesses, commands
and resolves; anything unmodelled is reported once under -d unimp.
